<p>From there, every new rule adds up. A portal with tens of thousands of SKUs, strict stock control, tiered prices with quantity steps, replenishment, buyer and agent roles and two carts running at once is not the same project: ${projectLink('ewheel-b2b', 'Ewheel')} has taken seven or eight months and is still going, with a backend team working on the same store. Most projects land in between, from four months upwards.</p>
<p>And a warning I would rather give before we start than after: of the time that gets lost along the way, 30 to 40% sits on your side. It goes on waiting for the real price lists, on deciding which company belongs to which tier, and on validating stock. Bring that settled and the portal lands at the low end of the range.</p>`,
